    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/event/come-from-away/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Come From Away"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Preview Dates: Tuesday, June 30 &amp; Thursday, July 2 Opening Date: Friday, July 3 Running Time: 1h 30 (No Intermission) Come From Away is based on the true story of a small town that welcomed the world. What started as an average day in Gander, Newfoundland turned into a historic moment when 38 planes carrying thousands of people were diverted there on September 11, 2001. Cultures clashed and nerves ran high, but the East Coast community welcomed these &#8220;come from aways&#8221; into their lives with open arms; uneasiness turned into trust, and gratitude grew into enduring friendships. Come From Away tells a heartwarming story of kindness in the face of unprecedented circumstances. AUDIENCE ADVISORY: Light haze effects are used in this production. PRE-SHOW CHATS Ticket-holders can get a behind-the-scenes peek at this year&#8217;s two Sobey Family Theatre musicals with Charlottetown Festival Artistic Director Adam Brazier. Learn about the rehearsal process, see images from the designs, and more during this interactive pre-show event. Come From AwayFriday, July 24 at 6:30 p.m. (duration 30 minutes) Anne of Green Gables – The Musical™Wednesday, August 5 at 6:30 p.m. (duration 30 minutes) POST-SHOW TALK-BACKS Every Thursday this summer, starting July 16, ticket holders are [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
