    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/fr/event/come-from-away/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Come From Away"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "A Confederation Centre of the Arts Production Preview Dates: Tuesday, June 30 &amp; Thursday, July 2 Opening Date: Friday, July 3 Running Time: 1h 30 (No Intermission) Come From Away is based on the true story of a small town that welcomed the world. What started as an average day in Gander, Newfoundland turned into a historic moment when 38 planes carrying thousands of people were diverted there on September 11, 2001. Cultures clashed and nerves ran high, but the East Coast community welcomed these &#8220;come from aways&#8221; into their lives with open arms; uneasiness turned into trust, and gratitude grew into enduring friendships. Come From Away tells a heartwarming story of kindness in the face of unprecedented circumstances. Book, Music, and Lyrics by Irene Sankoff and David Hein Presented through special arrangement with Music Theatre International (MTI). All authorized performance materials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com AUDIENCE ADVISORY: Light haze effects are used in this production. PRE-SHOW CHATS Ticket-holders can get a behind-the-scenes peek at this year&#8217;s two Sobey Family Theatre musicals with Charlottetown Festival Artistic Director Adam Brazier. Learn about the rehearsal process, see images from the designs, and more during this interactive pre-show event. Come From [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "On Stage, Theatre"
      }
    ],
